    A pure-QEMU run can now drain hybrid_state_v1 at the ROI exit boundary
    (exit_marker=1 for marker mode, exit_pc=0x... for pc mode), producing the
    reference the differential verifier compares against the vsim drain. The
    tick arms on the boundary insn and drains on the NEXT exec callback, so
    the capture equals vsim's post-retire record (DPC = next insn) even for a
    branching boundary insn. Exclusive with the other trigger modes.

